      "description": "Watch Manchester City vs Bournemouth highlights and goals from Premier League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 23, 2026. The atmosphere at the stadium was electric as Manchester City hosted Bournemouth on August 23, 2026. Fans gathered in their thousands to witness a high-stakes encounter in the Premier League International Cup . Bournemouth Stun the Hosts Despite Manchester City controlling much of the early possession, it was Bournemouth who struck first against the run of play. In the 26th minute, following a brilliant build-up involving Rayan , Evanilson found Marcus Tavernier , who clinicaly slotted the ball home with his left foot. The home side looked to respond immediately, with Erling Haaland forcing a save from Djordje Petrovic , but the visitors held firm. As the first half drew to a close, tensions rose, leading to a yellow card for Evanilson as the Cherries maintained their narrow lead. Late Surge and VAR Drama The second half saw Manchester City ramp up the pressure, eventually finishing with 66% possession. The introduction of Rayan Cherki proved to be the turning point. In the 84th minute, Cherki delivered a pinpoint corner that allowed Marc Guehi to power a header into the net for the equalizer. The momentum had firmly shifted, and the home side pushed for a winner as the clock ticked into stoppage time. In the 91st minute, the comeback was completed in dramatic fashion. Rayan Cherki provided his second assist of the match, setting up Josko Gvardiol for a close-range finish. The goal was initially met with a VAR check, causing a tense silence across the stadium before the referee officially awarded the goal. Despite late offside scares at both ends, the hosts held on to secure a thrilling victory in a match defined by its frantic final minutes."
